  m_text: "During a ward round, the specialty trainee asks you to ensure a patient
    receives a prescription of tocolytics (medication to suppress premature labour).
    You have begun to suspect this patient may have a placental abruption, which
    would be a contra-indication for this medication. The specialty trainee (registrar)
    has now left the ward.  \r\nWhich of the following actions is the most appropriate
    in this situation? \r\n"
